        <h3>Mechanics of breathing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Inhalation is active.</strong> The diaphragm contracts and flattens while external intercostals lift the ribs, increasing thoracic volume. By Boyle's law, increased volume means decreased pressure, so air flows in down its pressure gradient.</li>
